<p>France said Cécile Kohler and Jacques Paris, two French nationals detained in Iran since 2022, have been released and are traveling home, bringing an end to a detention case that had become a diplomatic dispute between Paris and Tehran. Iranian authorities arrested the pair while they were visiting the country as tourists and accused them of spying.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/9y8DzDKpGZgviz1_xZtzmHp_kekQ0cPDJu8JOyVOxIue8IcIXruitTQlCnA5Td6DXk9eK_CBuZs3vXtfsFKtxZSWw6-g8x866CeCMVdFVB5jYb8383r_yfs9sWfgMfnxxUnOiobQ0EtZ5ZWMJ6qMAZEp11eQQD84HcWmQ4zDZJsJg3K4pg' alt='Portraits of Cécile Kohler and Jacques Paris displayed on the gates of the Assemblée Nationale in Paris, March 11, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Public reaction: The New York Times said the case mobilized the French public and turned the couple&#x27;s detention into a long-running cause in France.</li><li>Detention length: The BBC reported that Kohler and Paris left Iran after more than three years in jail.</li><li>Exchange terms: Le Monde reported that, as part of the arrangement tied to the couple&#x27;s release, France lifted the house arrest of an Iranian woman convicted of online incitement to terrorism.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Iranian authorities: After the arrest, Iran accused the two French nationals of spying and presented the case as a security matter, not a wrongful detention. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/07/world/middleeast/iran-french-couple-freed.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Experts cited by Le Monde: Analysts described the release as a tactical gesture by Tehran, tied to broader diplomatic calculations involving France, the United States, and the conflict around Iran. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/08/iran-s-tactical-gesture-in-releasing-french-hostages-cecile-kohler-and-jacques-paris_6752205_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/08/iran-s-tactical-gesture-in-releasing-french-hostages-cecile-kohler-and-jacques-paris_6752205_4.html'>Iran&#x27;s &#x27;tactical gesture&#x27; in releasing French hostages Cécile Kohler and Jacques Paris</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/07/world/middleeast/iran-french-couple-freed.html'>Cécile Kohler and Jacques Paris, French Couple Held in Iran, Are Free</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/clyxk5640wko'>French couple leave Iran after more than three years in jail</a> - bbc.com</li></ul>